# DB Actions Patch-Day Runbook Sync

The super-admin **Game Data Update Process** in `src/components/DbActionsModal.tsx` must stay aligned with **`docs/DATA_SOURCES.md`** → section **Data Update Process** (`#data-update-process`).

## Source of truth

| Artifact | Role |
|----------|------|
| `docs/DATA_SOURCES.md` | Canonical patch-day runbook (prose + step order) |
| `DbActionsModal.tsx` → `PATCH_DAY_STEPS` | UI mirror: numbered steps, copy-paste commands, optional flags |
| `package.json` scripts | Every `npm run …` in the runbook must exist here |

## When to update both

Update **DATA_SOURCES.md and `PATCH_DAY_STEPS` in the same change** when:

- Adding, removing, or reordering patch-day steps
- Adding or renaming npm scripts used on patch day (`parse-game-data`, `patch-audit`, `fetch-shop-data`, etc.)
- Changing optional vs required steps (UEX refresh, BP Dumper, DFP engine)
- Moving sync/build/deploy ordering

## Checklist

- [ ] Step **numbers and order** match between doc and `PATCH_DAY_STEPS`
- [ ] Each doc step with a command has the same **`npm run …`** or **`.\\scripts\\…`** string in `commands[]`
- [ ] **Optional** steps are marked `optional: true` in UI and labeled optional in the doc
- [ ] Manual steps (verify removals, sync catalog button, commit/deploy) have **empty `commands`** but matching descriptions
- [ ] New npm scripts added to `package.json` and documented in DATA_SOURCES scripts table when relevant
- [ ] Footnote commands (e.g. `rebuild-mission-rewards`) mentioned in both places if patch-day troubleshooting changes

## Do not

- Drift the UI runbook from the doc — officers rely on DB Actions for patch day
- Duplicate the full runbook in README; link to `docs/DATA_SOURCES.md` instead
